{"context":"Steward spawns agent CLIs that run arbitrary commands. The existing plugin env allow-list (`pluginEnv`) inherits `PATH` AND `HOME`; HOME is `~/.eka` (the store), `~/.ssh`, `~/.aws`, agent-CLI credential dotfiles. A git worktree is VCS isolation, NOT a kernel confinement (same UID, unconfined FS, no landlock/seccomp/namespace). The store is a plain SQLite file at `~/.eka/eka.db` (mode 0644) reachable by any same-UID process; integrity only DETECTS edits. 'Checksum trust per ADR-028' is install-time and plugins-only, and does not cover arbitrary driver binaries on PATH.","decision":"Real containment in v1, stated honestly. (1) Workers do NOT inherit the host `HOME`: per-worker scratch HOME; the allow-list drops HOME. (2) Containment is OS-level and MANDATORY on Linux (landlock, or a distinct UID owning `~/.eka` with 0700); macOS via `sandbox-exec`, Windows deferred and documented. A git worktree is stated as VCS isolation, NOT a security boundary. (3) The sandbox backend is PLUGGABLE; microVM/gVisor is the required target on the v2 path. (4) The sole-writer invariant is enforced: workers cannot reach `~/.eka`, and `eka` authoring verbs are absent from worker PATH. (5) Permissions follow the ACP ADR (timeout=\u003edeny, normalized input, advisory-only). (6) Drivers are a trust boundary: known driver =\u003e pinned exact version + checksum, unknown =\u003e refused (extends ADR-028 beyond plugins). (7) Secrets are injected per-driver, least-privilege, never via `os.Environ()`, plus an egress policy. ADR-028 is scoped to registry apps only and does NOT satisfy (6).","consequences":"Workers cannot read host credentials or mutate the store by default; permission-requiring actions are denied until allowed. Safety is real, not asserted. Cost: sandbox setup, worktree lifecycle, a secrets broker and an egress policy; Linux-first parity.","alternativesConsidered":"Env allow-list + worktree as the sandbox (rejected: not confinement; HOME leak). Opt-in sandbox (rejected: unsafe default). Container/microVM-per-worker now (deferred to the pluggable backend's v2 default target: heavier). Convention-only sole-writer (rejected: unenforceable)."}